       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Amlodipine's maximum recommended dose is 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg, and 100 mg is 10 times that maximum. At that dose, a 70 kg adult could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and shock. Calcium channel blocker overdose can also cause noncardiogenic pulmonary edema, and it is hard to treat.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily (the maximum dose)\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily (a common starting or maintenance dose)\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily (a lower starting dose, sometimes used in frail patients)\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 100 mg, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale. I can add that to the order note, but I'd want you to confirm it first."
